# The trailer, a teaser then a tutorial, about a minute and a half: a finished plan shown off; two community plans
# built again by the tour's cursor without NEI (no recipe pages flashing by), sped up, each followed by a slow tilted
# pan over the finished plan (looking up and to the left); then the features one by one, from the tour played with no
# notes of its own, a typed caption each; the minimap in its corner over a real world; the owner's own clip of laying a
# plan out in the world; the name.
# Cut to the approved café track (cafe.mjs, 112 BPM, a bar is 4b = 2.142857 s), lengthened for the ending by playing its
# bars 24 to 33 twice: the band to 72b, the easy half to 192b, the end from 192b (bar 48).
#   node tools/trailer/splice.mjs build/trailer/cafe-approved.wav build/trailer/cafe-long.wav 112 0-2,18-38,2-18,29-34,2-18,38-end
#   java -Xmx10g tools/trailer/Trailer.java tools/trailer/trailer.shot [--stills | --every 1]
#
# Footage (run/client/recordings/, from the dev harness; see README.md): tour3 (call 'tutorial?quiet=1', 4K at GUI
# scale 4), nitro3 and plat3 (call 'rebuild?file=...&nei=0', 4K), minimap4 (the minimap in its corner in a normal world, panned and zoomed;
# filmed from a worktree at the last commit); the
# pictures are plans' own (call planpicture): the tour's plan at the Arrange step, and the two finished rebuilds.

size 1920 1080
fps 60
bpm 112
duration 133.1
source run/client/recordings/tour3-1080
out build/trailer/trailer.mp4
stilldir build/trailer/stills
set audio build/trailer/cafe-long.wav
set audiogain -3dB
set audiofade 2.5
# The encode on the graphics card (NVENC), the CPU left to rendering.
set encoder nvenc

title GTNH Planner
subtitle Now in game.
set wordscale 11
set subscale 4
set subgap 34
set dotstep 40
set dotsize 4
set captionscale 4
# Clear of the overview on the left.
set captionx 232
set typespeed 30
set badgemarginx 360
set badgemarginy 64

# The picture as it is: no vignette, bloom, depth of field or grain.
set vignette 0
set bloom 0
set grain 0
set focusr 5
set blendframes 0
set dissolve 0.3
key exposure 0 0
key exposure 0.8 1

# Shown off where nothing moves: the tour's tower and turbine, a steady pan across them.
shot 0 8b showcase
  source run/client/screenshots/Plan_2_2026-10-10_15.05.45.png
  set linear 1
  key zoom 0 1.02
  key zoom 8b 1.06
  key cx 0 0.555
  key cx 8b 0.76
  key cy 0 0.5
  set dissolve 0
end
say 0.7 3.9 This is *GTNH Planner*.

# The tutorial: the tour as it played, without its notes; waits between steps skipped.
shot 8b 16b nei
  remap 0 2.9
  remap 2.2 5.7
  remap 2.3 7.4
  remap 8b 9.95
  key zoom 0 1
end
say 8b+0.1 16b-0.35 Find a recipe in *NEI*, then hit the *plan button*.

shot 16b 22b drawers
  src 12.4 16.9
  key zoom 0 1
end
say 16b+0.1 22b-0.35 Drag out its *inputs* and *outputs*.

shot 22b 28b rate
  remap 0 17.6
  remap 1.2 18.8
  remap 1.25 19.5
  remap 6b 21.7
  key zoom 0 1
end
say 22b+0.1 28b-0.35 Set a *rate*, and the rest works itself out.

shot 28b 32b tier
  src 22.3 24.6
  key zoom 0 1
end
say 28b+0.1 32b-0.35 Set the *tier* and *amps*.

shot 32b 40b clone
  remap 0 29.3
  remap 1.75 31.7
  remap 1.8 32.7
  remap 8b 35.5
  key zoom 0 1
end
say 32b+0.1 40b-0.35 *Clone* a card, or run two recipes on *one machine*.

shot 40b 48b fromnei
  remap 0 47.4
  remap 1.75 51.0
  remap 1.8 52.45
  remap 8b 57.25
  key zoom 0 1
end
say 40b+0.1 48b-0.35 Drag things in from *NEI*, or press *R* or *U* on anything.

shot 48b 54b leftovers
  remap 0 58.0
  remap 1.6 60.5
  remap 1.65 61.5
  remap 6b 62.6
  key zoom 0 1
end
say 48b+0.1 54b-0.35 Leftovers can be *byproducts* or *trash*.

shot 54b 66b power
  remap 0 63.4
  remap 0.6 64.2
  remap 0.65 65.95
  remap 12b 76.9
  key zoom 0 1
end
say 54b+0.1 66b-0.35 Plan your *power* too.

shot 66b 70b arrange
  src 79.6 82.2
  key zoom 0 1
end
say 66b+0.1 70b-0.35 *Arrange* tidies it up.

shot 70b 80b notes
  src 84.0 92.9
  key zoom 0 1
end
say 70b+0.1 80b-0.35 Leave yourself *sticky notes*.

# The library reloads as the tour types its search; this is the stretch its tiles all show, held.
shot 80b 88b library
  src 98.4 98.95
  set blendframes 1
  key zoom 0 1
end
say 80b+0.1 88b-0.35 Grab setups other players have *shared*.

# A power plant from the library, built again by the cursor, the whole screen, sped up.
shot 88b 108b nitro
  source run/client/recordings/nitro3-1080
  remap 0 3.0
  remap 0.6 5.5
  remap 9.9 153.0
  remap 20b 157.4
  set shutter 1
  key zoom 0 1
end
say 88b+0.6 88b+5.2 Plan a whole *power plant*...
badge 88b+0.2 108b-0.2 *14x* speed

# The finished plant, tilted, looking up and to the left, a slow pan from its fuel to its turbines.
shot 108b 116b nitropan
  source run/client/screenshots/Plan_2_2026-10-10_16.44.22.png
  set linear 1
  key roll 0 -2.5
  key yaw 0 8
  key pitch 0 -6
  key zoom 0 2.4
  key zoom 8b 2.1
  key cx 0 0.24
  key cx 8b 0.74
  key cy 0 0.27
  key cy 8b 0.40
end

# The Platline, built again, the whole screen, sped up.
shot 116b 144b platline
  source run/client/recordings/plat3-1080
  remap 0 3.0
  remap 0.6 5.0
  remap 14.2 353.0
  remap 28b 356.0
  set shutter 1
  key zoom 0 1
end
say 116b+0.7 116b+4.6 ...or a whole *Platline*.
badge 116b+0.3 144b-0.2 *24x* speed

# The finished line, tilted the same way, a slow pan as it pulls back.
shot 144b 152b platpan
  source run/client/screenshots/Plan_2_2026-10-10_16.50.23.png
  set linear 1
  key roll 0 -2.5
  key yaw 0 8
  key pitch 0 -6
  key zoom 0 1.75
  key zoom 8b 1.4
  key cx 0 0.28
  key cx 8b 0.64
  key cy 0 0.36
  key cy 8b 0.40
end
say 144b+0.3 152b-0.4 Plan it all before you *build* it.

# The world, the whole screen, then a move in toward the minimap in its corner (toward it, not onto it), held there
# while it pans and zooms.
shot 152b 172b minimap
  source run/client/recordings/minimap4
  src 0.4 11.1
  key zoom 0 1
  key zoom 1.6 1
  key zoom 3.8 1.3
  key cx 0 0.5
  key cx 1.6 0.5
  key cx 3.8 0.615
  key cy 0 0.5
  key cy 1.6 0.5
  key cy 3.8 0.385
end
say 152b+2.4 162b-0.35 Your plan follows you on the *minimap*.
say 162b+0.1 172b-0.35 Pan and zoom it while you play.

# The owner's clip of laying a plan out in the world (no sound), all of it, sped up to sixteen bars.
shot 172b 236b inworld
  source run/client/recordings/inworld
  src 0.1 49.2
  set shutter 1
  key zoom 0 1
end
say 172b+8.4 172b+13.5 You can also lay out a plan in the *world*.

# The name, faded up from the clip, as the music ends.
shot 236b 133.1 end
  source run/client/recordings/inworld
  src 49.2 49.3
  key zoom 0 1
  key endbg 0 0
  key endbg 1.0 1
  key endcard 0.6 0
  key endcard 1.9 1
  # The subtitle drops in on the beat a bar after the music's last hit.
  key endsub 4b 0
  key endsub 4b+0.16 1
  key master 4.6 1
  key master 6.4 0
  set dissolve 0.6
end

still 2
still 6
still 30
still 46
still 49
still 60
still 80
still 84
still 95
still 110
still 128.5
